# Line endings are part of the submission contract, not a style preference.
#
# The team works on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file Git rewrites
# run.sh to CRLF on checkout, the builder packs it as it finds it, and the target
# Linux runner reports `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter` -- a zero on every task at once.
# scripts/check_submission.py verifies the built archive as well, because a .gitattributes
# only helps the people who have it.

* text=auto eol=lf

run.sh text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

*.zip binary
*.docx binary
